ng, ObjParser readers and writers, geometry3Sharp's OBJ/OFF/STL/SVG readers and writers, StlProcessing) names the invariant culture at each number instead of swapping the thread's culture, and CA1304, CA1305 and CA1311 are errors in the I/O folders so stored text cannot lean on the thread's culture again. MATTERCAD_TEST_CULTURE (de-DE, fr-FR, tr-TR...) sets the culture of a whole Agg.Tests run, with a CultureScope helper for tests that switch it. DisplayNumber is the one helper that formats a shown number (never grouped) and reads a typed one (invariant first, then the culture), refusing an ambiguous thousands-grouped whole number (\"1.000\" under de-DE, \"1,000\" under en-US) rather than guessing. InternalNumberEdit shows its number in the user's culture and keeps its last value when committed text cannot be read. A relative date shows the time in the culture's own short time format (\"15:13\" in de-DE, not \"3:13 PM\").","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"LuxAlgo/PineTS","commit_timestamp":"2026-09-30T20:38:35Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"8c623740340e8abdabf77e4302184c7e4705e43a","github_link":"https://github.com/LuxAlgo/PineTS/commit/8c623740340e8abdabf77e4302184c7e4705e43a","commit_subject":"Arrays as on TradingView: slice views, sorts, na in statistics, element equality, runtime errors, defaults","ai_tool":"Cursor"},{"repo_name":"apache/tomcat","commit_timestamp":"2026-09-30T20:38:26Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"6062ded9a0da5141c8a47bd6febf8d496eaa1fd3","github_link":"https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/6062ded9a0da5141c8a47bd6febf8d496eaa1fd3","commit_subject":"Bound connect and read operations in TcpSender with timeouts since the heartbeat runs on the shared server utility executor, and close connections on read failure","ai_tool":"OpenCode"},{"repo_name":"CircleCI-Public/circleci-yaml-language-server","commit_timestamp":"2026-09-30T20:38:17Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"e611b9cae08af4238bddbf30e37877531e90e335","github_link":"https://github.com/Ci